    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** and **Trea Turner** headlining our lineup as elite-tier starts. **Yordan Alvarez** projects for a massive 81.37, bolstered by an elite 0.450 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Pfaadt. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (78.93) is a priority start, leveraging a high-volume spot in the two-hole against the vulnerable P\u00e9rez. Our stolen base strategy remains front and center with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (75.78), who carries a dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the necessary green light to exploit Gusto\u2019s defensive vulnerabilities, solidifying his role as a key contributor to our league-leading speed metrics despite the minor penalty for opposing battery efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Kazuma Okamoto**, whose 58.20 score narrowly edged out our bench options. While **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a tricky right-on-right matchup against Lugo, his high SP skill adjustment (+14%) kept him in the UTIL spot over potential deep-bench contributors like **Casey Schmitt** or **Luis Pena**, who were considered for their high-contact profiles but lacked the raw scoring efficiency today. We are monitoring **Junior Caminero** closely; while his 55.11 score suggests he is a viable start, he faces a daunting matchup against deGrom. The -19% SP skill penalty is significant, but his slot in the three-hole and positive platoon indicators keep him active. Investors should note that while **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, and **Josh Smith** are unavailable, we remain well-positioned to maximize our daily game caps with **Hector Rodriguez** and **Lars Nootbaar** providing excellent stability at the top of the order.",
